se trains (externally controlled); pin to the nearest aligned upstream build and record the deviation.\n\nWait — the AC \"pipeline green\" — the konflux epic E003 delivers the pipeline. E002's AC references the platform's build pipeline without naming E003. Good — no cross-reference.\n\nE003 (konflux-onboarding):\n\n# Konflux build pipeline for the vLLM ROCm runtime image\n\n## Description\nExtends the existing Konflux onboarding of the midstream vLLM repository with the build pipeline recipe for the new ROCm runtime image variant, so the image is built, tested, and released through the platform's standard pipeline rather than ad hoc.\n\n## Scope\n- Add the ROCm image variant to the repository's Konflux build configuration (known-recipe pipeline work).\n- Configure build and test tasks applicable to the ROCm variant.\n- Verify the pipeline produces the ROCm image with the expected provenance/attestations.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- The Konflux pipeline builds the ROCm vLLM runtime image variant and completes green.\n- The image is produced with standard release artifacts (attestations/provenance) matching the existing CUDA variant's pipeline outputs.\n\n## HLR Traceability\n- HLR-2 (P0): productization of the supported vLLM ROCm serving runtime (build/release pipeline aspect).\n\nRuns in parallel with runtime image/productization work — coupling is via the \"pipeline green\" acceptance criterion on that work, not a dependency. Hmm — careful: \"no cross-references to sibling epics\" — saying \"runtime image/productization work\" in plain terms is fine.\n\nE004 (Training Operator):\n\n# PyTorch training on ROCm via PyTorchJob\n\n## Description\nEnables PyTorch training on AMD Instinct accelerators for single- and multi-GPU jobs submitted as PyTorchJobs, using ROCm-based PyTorch execution environments.\n\n## Scope\n- Support PyTorchJob execution on AMD GPU nodes with ROCm PyTorch images (worker pods with amd.com/gpu resources).\n- Validate single-GPU and multi-GPU (m