 (functional correctness) through the productized runtime on AMD Instinct\n  hardware.\n- The supported/validated model list recorded for the ROCm runtime matches the\n  campaign's go/no-go scope.\n\n## HLR Traceability\n\n- HLR-2 (P0): a supported vLLM ROCm serving runtime is productized for the\n  models the validation campaign clears.\n\n## Risks / Notes\n\n- Scope is defined by the validation campaign's go/no-go report: a reduced\n  cleared list reduces scope; a full no-go removes the productization in favor\n  of handing off the campaign findings.\n- Upstream ROCm image release cadence may not align with platform release\n  trains (externally controlled by AMD and the upstream communities); pin to\n  the nearest aligned upstream build and record the deviation.\n"}}],"model":"rits/zai-org/glm-5-3","stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":54959,"output_tokens":0},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-95ba045d32a00c6b","agent_id":"aed3d9bc59117f76c","session_id":"ca1a66b0-be22-44b3-9715-c3e9690708e5","uuid":"96c75a1c-ee13-4fa6-92a6-470a721c9ba6","timestamp":"2026-10-26T08:43:39.876Z","subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Decompose RHAISTRAT-9020"}
