{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-bff73bd4b7690644","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tepic_id: RHAISTRAT-9020-E003\n3\ttitle: Konflux build pipeline for the vLLM ROCm runtime image\n4\tparent_strat: RHAISTRAT-9020\n5\tcomponent: Serving Runtimes\n6\tteam: RHOAI Serving\n7\ttype: Implementation\n8\tpriority: P0\n9\timplementation_type: konflux-onboarding\n10\tdependencies: []\n11\tai_signals:\n12\t  change_specificity: 1\n13\t  pattern_precedent: 1\n14\t  adapter_pattern: 0\n15\t  existing_foundation: 1\n16\t  open_questions: 1\n17\t  external_dependency: 0\n18\t  human_process_gates: 0\n19\t  repo_access: 1\n20\t  architecture_claims: 1\n21\tinvestigation_signals: null\n22\tai_implementability: High\n23\tai_implementability_score: 6\n24\tjira_key: null\n25\tbranch: null\n26\tgated_by: null\n27\tgate_failure_impact: null\n28\t---\n29\t# Konflux build pipeline for the vLLM ROCm runtime image\n30\t\n31\t## Description\n32\t\n33\tExtends the existing Konflux onboarding of the midstream vLLM repository with\n34\tthe build pipeline recipe for the new ROCm runtime image variant, so the image\n35\tis built, tested, and released through the platform's standard pipeline with\n36\tthe same release artifacts as the CUDA variants. This is known-recipe pipeline\n37\twork for a new container image in an already-onboarded repository, and it runs\n38\tin parallel with the runtime image build and productization work — the coupling\n39\t(the ROCm image being released green through this pipeline) is expressed as an\n40\tacceptance criterion on that work, not as a dependency.\n41\t\n42\t## Scope\n43\t\n44\t- Add the ROCm image variant to the repository's Konflux build configuration.\n45\t- Configure the build and test tasks applicable to the ROCm variant.\n46\t- Verify the pipeline produces the ROCm image with the expected provenance and\n47\t  attestations, matching the existing CUDA variant's pipeline outputs.\n48\t\n49\t## Acceptance Criteria\n50\t\n51\t- The Konflux pipeline builds the vLLM ROCm runtime image variant and completes\n52\t  green.\n53\t- The image is produced with the standard release artifacts (signed\n54\t  attestations/provenance) matching the existing CUDA variant's pipeline\n55\t  outputs.\n56\t\n57\t## HLR Traceability\n58\t\n59\t- HLR-2 (P0): a supported vLLM ROCm serving runtime is productized for the\n60\t  cleared models — this epic delivers its build/release pipeline aspect.\n61\t\n62\t## Risks / Notes\n63\t\n64\t- Proceeds in parallel with the validation campaign and the runtime\n65\t  productization; it is outcome-independent known-recipe work, but its value is\n66\t  contingent on the campaign clearing at least some models.\n67\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-89db8f0f5a287418","agent_id":"ab1e96f21a74eab04","session_id":"ca1a66b0-be22-44b3-9715-c3e9690708e5","uuid":"a668a213-6b08-4a9a-a381-3182e246db99","timestamp":"2026-10-26T08:47:06.946Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-bff73bd4b7690644","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Review RHAISTRAT-9020 decomposition"}
