{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-9ee2cdf8f2ae003f","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tepic_id: RHAISTRAT-9020-E004\n3\ttitle: PyTorch training on ROCm via PyTorchJob\n4\tparent_strat: RHAISTRAT-9020\n5\tcomponent: Training Operator\n6\tteam: Distributed Workloads\n7\ttype: Implementation\n8\tpriority: P1\n9\tdependencies: []\n10\tai_signals:\n11\t  change_specificity: 0\n12\t  pattern_precedent: 1\n13\t  adapter_pattern: 0\n14\t  existing_foundation: 1\n15\t  open_questions: 0\n16\t  external_dependency: -1\n17\t  human_process_gates: 0\n18\t  repo_access: 1\n19\t  architecture_claims: 1\n20\timplementation_type: null\n21\tinvestigation_signals: null\n22\tai_implementability: High\n23\tai_implementability_score: 3\n24\tjira_key: null\n25\tbranch: null\n26\tgated_by: null\n27\tgate_failure_impact: null\n28\t---\n29\t# PyTorch training on ROCm via PyTorchJob\n30\t\n31\t## Description\n32\t\n33\tEnables PyTorch training on AMD Instinct accelerators for single- and\n34\tmulti-GPU jobs submitted as PyTorchJobs, using ROCm-based PyTorch execution\n35\tenvironments. This is the Training Operator side of the strategy's training\n36\trequirement; queueing and quota handling for these jobs is tracked separately\n37\tunder Distributed Workloads and coordinated via acceptance criteria rather than\n38\ta dependency.\n39\t\n40\t## Scope\n41\t\n42\t- Support PyTorchJob execution on AMD GPU nodes with ROCm PyTorch images,\n43\t  including worker pods that request amd.com/gpu resources.\n44\t- Validate single-GPU and multi-GPU (multi-worker) PyTorchJob topologies on\n45\t  AMD Instinct hardware.\n46\t- Validate compatible upstream ROCm PyTorch image usage for training jobs and\n47\t  record the compatible image guidance.\n48\t\n49\t## Acceptance Criteria\n50\t\n51\t- A single-GPU PyTorchJob using a ROCm PyTorch image completes training\n52\t  successfully on AMD Instinct nodes.\n53\t- A multi-GPU (distributed, multi-worker) PyTorchJob completes training\n54\t  successfully on AMD Instinct nodes.\n55\t- Jobs correctly request and receive amd.com/gpu resources on AMD GPU nodes.\n56\t\n57\t## HLR Traceability\n58\t\n59\t- HLR-3 (P1): PyTorch training on ROCm is supported for single- and multi-GPU\n60\t  jobs admitted through Kueue, with amd.com/gpu quota handling — this epic\n61\t  covers the PyTorchJob execution side.\n62\t\n63\t## Risks / Notes\n64\t\n65\t- Requires AMD Instinct hardware for validation; hardware access is secured\n66\t  through the validation campaign's procurement/partner-lab engagement, so\n67\t  scheduling must be coordinated (coordination risk, not a dependency).\n68\t- Upstream ROCm PyTorch image release cadence is controlled by AMD and the\n69\t  upstream communities; image availability may not align with platform release\n70\t  trains.\n71\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-89db8f0f5a287418","agent_id":"ab1e96f21a74eab04","session_id":"ca1a66b0-be22-44b3-9715-c3e9690708e5","uuid":"47ff5e7a-4705-4a48-90d9-df124fea0eaa","timestamp":"2026-10-26T08:47:07.951Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-9ee2cdf8f2ae003f","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Review RHAISTRAT-9020 decomposition"}
