{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-9820ba76770017b9","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tepic_id: RHAISTRAT-9020-E002\n3\ttitle: Productize the vLLM ROCm serving runtime\n4\tparent_strat: RHAISTRAT-9020\n5\tcomponent: Serving Runtimes\n6\tteam: RHOAI Serving\n7\ttype: Implementation\n8\tpriority: P0\n9\tdependencies:\n10\t- RHAISTRAT-9020-E001\n11\tgated_by: RHAISTRAT-9020-E001\n12\tgate_failure_impact:\n13\t  action: remove\n14\t  fallback_approach: On a full no-go (no model clears), remove the productization\n15\t    epic and hand off the campaign findings report; on a partial clear, rewrite the\n16\t    productization scope to the cleared model list.\n17\tai_signals:\n18\t  change_specificity: 0\n19\t  pattern_precedent: 1\n20\t  adapter_pattern: 0\n21\t  existing_foundation: 1\n22\t  open_questions: 0\n23\t  external_dependency: -1\n24\t  human_process_gates: 0\n25\t  repo_access: 1\n26\t  architecture_claims: 1\n27\timplementation_type: null\n28\tinvestigation_signals: null\n29\tai_implementability: High\n30\tai_implementability_score: 3\n31\tjira_key: null\n32\tbranch: null\n33\t---\n34\t# Productize the vLLM ROCm serving runtime\n35\t\n36\t## Description\n37\t\n38\tBuilds and productizes a supported vLLM ROCm serving runtime for the models\n39\tcleared by the validation campaign — the platform's first supported AMD\n40\taccelerator serving runtime, extending the existing CUDA-only productized\n41\truntime family. Scope is defined by the campaign's go/no-go report: only the\n42\tmodels it clears are productized.\n43\t\n44\t## Scope\n45\t\n46\t- Build the vLLM ROCm runtime container image in the existing midstream vLLM\n47\t  repository, based on upstream ROCm builds.\n48\t- Define and productize the ServingRuntime (or ClusterServingRuntime) for the\n49\t  ROCm variant so it can be selected for KServe InferenceServices, including\n50\t  amd.com/gpu resource handling and node placement on AMD Instinct nodes.\n51\t- Validate the productized runtime end-to-end under KServe InferenceServices\n52\t  on AMD Instinct hardware for the cleared model set. This covers the KServe\n53\t  component of the strategy, which requires no code changes: InferenceServices\n54\t  must schedule and serve correctly with the ROCm runtime and amd.com/gpu\n55\t  resources.\n56\t- Release enablement for the cleared model list, including the supported model\n57\t  list record for the ROCm runtime.\n58\t\n59\t## Acceptance Criteria\n60\t\n61\t- A vLLM ROCm serving runtime image is built in the midstream repository and\n62\t  released green through the platform's Konflux build pipeline (the ROCm image\n63\t  variant included).\n64\t- The runtime is deployable as a ServingRuntime under KServe InferenceServices\n65\t  with amd.com/gpu resources on AMD Instinct nodes.\n66\t- Every model on the validation campaign's cleared list serves successfully\n67\t  (functional correctness) through the productized runtime on AMD Instinct\n68\t  hardware.\n69\t- The supported/validated model list recorded for the ROCm runtime matches the\n70\t  campaign's go/no-go scope.\n71\t\n72\t## HLR Traceability\n73\t\n74\t- HLR-2 (P0): a supported vLLM ROCm serving runtime is productized for the\n75\t  models the validation campaign clears.\n76\t\n77\t## Risks / Notes\n78\t\n79\t- Scope is defined by the validation campaign's go/no-go report: a reduced\n80\t  cleared list reduces scope; a full no-go removes the productization in favor\n81\t  of handing off the campaign findings.\n82\t- Upstream ROCm image release cadence may not align with platform release\n83\t  trains (externally controlled by AMD and the upstream communities); pin to\n84\t  the nearest aligned upstream build and record the deviation.\n85\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-a6b45b48e303b262","agent_id":"a588a9abb0bab51e1","session_id":"ca1a66b0-be22-44b3-9715-c3e9690708e5","uuid":"e0d9a0ff-e3c8-4d72-a606-9316bce112b4","timestamp":"2026-10-26T08:53:29.9